1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,505
Organizations are adding AI to more business applications every quarter.

2
00:00:05,505 --> 00:00:07,525
And a pattern is emerging.

3
00:00:07,525 --> 00:00:11,805
Most of those applications need the same AI capabilities.

4
00:00:11,805 --> 00:00:20,795
Whether it is case management, analytics, knowledge management, a CRM, or a legacy system, they all need the same foundations.

5
00:00:20,795 --> 00:00:21,830
Retrieval.

6
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:22,979
Analytics.

7
00:00:22,979 --> 00:00:24,166
Orchestration.

8
00:00:24,166 --> 00:00:25,479
Access control.

9
00:00:25,479 --> 00:00:26,464
Governance.

10
00:00:26,464 --> 00:00:30,820
Many organizations rebuild all of that application by application.

11
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:37,992
Every rebuild adds engineering effort, adds cost, and adds one more thing to govern.

12
00:00:37,992 --> 00:00:42,664
Ask-AI MCP Service offers another architectural approach.

13
00:00:42,664 --> 00:00:55,984
Ask-AI MCP Service provides those capabilities once, as a shared MCP service that applications simply connect to, while each application keeps its own business logic, workflows, and data.

14
00:00:55,984 --> 00:01:08,573
Inside Ask-AI MCP Service: retrieval augmented generation, analytics and graph agents, workflow orchestration, governance, access control, auditing, and model management.

15
00:01:08,573 --> 00:01:11,729
The goal is not to standardize every application.

16
00:01:11,729 --> 00:01:18,371
It is to standardize the AI capabilities that almost every application already requires.

17
00:01:18,371 --> 00:01:28,585
As AI adoption accelerates, the key architectural question may not be which model to use, but where AI belongs within the enterprise architecture.

18
00:01:28,585 --> 00:01:34,936
